{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a756a4ab3711a651","name":"Duros","source":{"id":"source:reference-a756a4ab3711a651","title":"Duros","revision":18349,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T19:59:52Z","sha256":"03feb31f258ac33770df8a4ed792ca82c40186c0744b4de3fdde645e2c985de8","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18349","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Duros&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a756a4ab3711a651","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Tall, hairless humanoids from the Duro System, Duros were one of the first Species to become a major influence in the Galactic Republic, and many respected scholars credited the Duros with creating the first ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"},". The Duros have a natural affinity for space travel, possessing an innate grasp of the mathematical underpinnings of astrogational computations. Many tales are swapped in cantinas about Duros astrogators calculating the coordinates for supposedly impossible jumps in their heads. Although not as numerous as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humans"},", the Duros are almost as omnipresent; all but the smallest settlements in known space feature Duros populations.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Duros Species has existed on other worlds in isolation from the rest of their kind, evolving in slight different directions from the baseline Species. The most populous and well-known near-Duros ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," are the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Neimoidians"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Neimoidians"},", a people rarely encountered during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebellion Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebellion_Era"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Duros Characteristics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Personality:"]}," A Duros tends to be intense and adventurous, always seeking to learn what's at the end of the next hyperspace jump. They are a proud, self-sufficient, fun-loving people who also have a tendency toward gregariousness.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Physical Description:"]}," Duros average about 1.8 meters tall and 70 kilograms. They are hairless, with large eyes and wide, lipless mouths. Skin color ranges from blue-gray to deep azure.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Age Groups"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Age_Groups"},":"]}," Duros age at the following stages:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHILD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["YOUNG ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MIDDLE AGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["OLD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["VENERABLE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1-9 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10-14 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["15-35 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["36-49 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["50-69 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["70+ Years\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Homeworld:"]}," The orbiting cities of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Duro"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Duro","referenceId":"reference:649f085c70b1304a"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Duros speak, read, and write both Durese and Basic.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Example Names:"]}," Baniss Keeg, Elior, Kadlo, Kir Vantai, Lai Nootka, Monnda Tebbo.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Adventurers:"]}," Duros adventurers include hyperspace explorers, star charters, and spacers of all descriptions as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scouts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scouts"},". Some Duros shun exploration in favor of smuggling and trading as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrels"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrels"},", and a small number go into diplomatic professions as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nobles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nobles"},". They also tend to gravitate toward the sciences, including engineering and astrogation.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Duros Species Traits"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Duros share the following Species Traits:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Ability Modifiers:"]}," Duros have a +2 bonus to both ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"},", and suffer a -2 penalty to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Constitution"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Constitution"},". Duros are agile in mind and body but they aren't physically hardy people."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Medium Size:"]}," As medium creatures, Duros have no special bonuses or penalties due to their size."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Duros have a base speed of 6 squares."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Expert Pilot:"]}," As natural spacers, a Duros may choose to reroll any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted even if it is worse."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Automatic Languages:"]}," All Duros can speak, read, and write both Basic and Durese."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Duros Species Feats"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Duros characters have access to the following ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species_Feats"},". No Species Feats are considered Bonus Feats for any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Class"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Class"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SPECIES FEAT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["BENEFITS\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Flawless Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flawless_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:c5b912d91555f1f8"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Reroll ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," checks, always keeping the better result.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Spacer's Surge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spacer%27s_Surge","referenceId":"reference:b13e0eb820f11d6d"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gain a temporary ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," when you roll a Natural 20 on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Veteran Spacer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Veteran_Spacer","referenceId":"reference:2b1174b48b9d36b1"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gain a bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," checks made to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Astrogate"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Astrogate"},".\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
